<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-anchiornis-huxleyi-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Anchiornis huxleyi Turing wavenumber at 2.0 nm (Late Jurassic, 160.0 Ma) — Code-to-model traceability: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The module docstring states the PDE, the parameters, the 2.0 nm calibration, the 160.0 Ma age, and the claim boundary. jacobian, dispersion_sigma, critical_wavenumber, and linear_growth_fit map onto those equations. The Lean file names the same integers (a=62/1000, b=1280/1000, Du=720/1000, Dv=31500/1000). Deduction: Lean proves scaled integer inequalities, not the floating-point eigenvalue in Lean itself." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-anchiornis-huxleyi-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-anchiornis-huxleyi-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-anchiornis-huxleyi-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Anchiornis huxleyi Turing wavenumber at 2.0 nm (Late Jurassic, 160.0 Ma) — Model fidelity to source: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The script implements the Schnakenberg steady state, Jacobian, dispersion eigenvalue, critical wavenumber, and unstable band, and checks det=(a+b)^2. Five Lean theorems (0 sorry) fix the trace sign, the positive determinant, Dv/Du>40, k_c inside the rounded band, and the 29 nm versus 2 nm scale step. Deduction: Li et al. 2010 do not contain this PDE; the kinetics are a reconstruction pinned to Turing 1952 and Schnakenberg 1979." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-anchiornis-huxleyi-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-anchiornis-huxleyi-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-anchiornis-huxleyi-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

