<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-anchiornis-huxleyi-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Anchiornis huxleyi Turing wavenumber at 2.0 nm (Late Jurassic, 160.0 Ma) (Anchiornis huxleyi)",
        "Anchiornis huxleyi Turing wavenumber at 2.0 nm (Late Jurassic, 160.0 Ma) faithfully reproduces Anchiornis huxleyi morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-anchiornis-huxleyi-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-anchiornis-huxleyi-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-anchiornis-huxleyi-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-anchiornis-huxleyi-turing-wavelength-s0-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-anchiornis-huxleyi-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Anchiornis huxleyi specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-anchiornis-huxleyi-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Anchiornis huxleyi" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: That Schnakenberg kinetics are the Anchiornis melanin pathway.",
        "does_not_claim: That a successor chronospecies of Anchiornis exists in this series.",
        "does_not_claim: That slot 1229 parameters were copied. That slot publishes none.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Equal-diffusion ablation, Dv sweep, and pure-mode growth-rate fit.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Final GIF frame: holotype photograph times a weak function of the simulated field.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Length unit that places analytical lambda_c at 2.0e-9 m.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg kinetics and the dispersion relation, with parameters chosen for this 2.0 nm detail slot.",
        "reported_in_source: Li et al. 2010: melanosome shape is the evidence for Anchiornis plumage color. Organelle lengths are hundreds of nanometres.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952: a critical wavenumber k_c when the inhibitor diffuses sufficiently faster than the activator.",
        "reported_in_source: Watt, Bothma and Meredith 2009: eumelanin is a stacked oligomeric sheet at nanometre scale.",
        "reported_in_source: Xu et al. 2009: Anchiornis huxleyi holotype IVPP V14378, Tiaojishan Formation, pennaceous feathers on forelimbs and hindlimbs.",
        "transfer_boundary: 2.0 nm is the assigned detail scale identified with the melanin sheet mode. Li et al. 2010 did not measure 2.0 nm.",
        "transfer_boundary: The museum photograph is not a 2 nm micrograph. Image fitness compares the registered final frame to that photograph." ;
